        "id": "R-privacy-1",
        "line": 11,
        "location": "src/logger.ts:3",
        "raisedBy": [
          "privacy"
        ],
        "recommendation": "The local-part and domain classes are ASCII-only, so any address with an accented or other non-ASCII character fails to match and is written to the logs unmasked: `logInfo(\"signup\", { email: \"josé@example.fr\" })` prints `\"email\":\"josé@example.fr\"`, and `ada@exämple.org` likewise passes through. Local parts with other legal characters leak a prefix (`o'brien@example.com` becomes `o'b***@example.com`). These customers' addresses then reach the hosting provider's logs, kept 90 days (GDPR Art. 5(1)(c) and (f), Art. 32), contrary to the release note. Match on `\\S+@\\S+`-style boundaries (or Unicode classes with the `u` flag, e.g. `[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+`) and add tests for a non-ASCII local part, a non-ASCII domain and an apostrophe.",
        "reported": true,
        "role": "privacy",
        "severity": "high",
        "status": "open",
        "step": "code.review",
        "title": "Addresses with non-ASCII characters are logged in full"
      },
