        ],
        "recommendation": "The logs keep the first letter of the local part and the whole domain. For a personal or small-company domain (`a***@lovelace-family.org`), that is enough to single out the customer, so the log line stays personal data (GDPR Art. 4(1), Art. 5(1)(c)). Depends on the customers' domains, which the reviewer could not see. Ask the team whether the domain is needed for diagnosis; if not, replace the whole address with a fixed token or a keyed hash.",
